      "topic": "staff",
      "sentiment": "positive",
      "mentions": 26,
      "title": {
        "en": "Attentive and reassuring urgent care team"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Many pet owners praise Dr Paz, Dr Halsey, and the receptionists, particularly Marty, for their warmth and emotional support during stressful emergencies. Reviewers highlight clear clinical explanations and comforting bedside manners when handling critically ill animals. Whilst two clients felt staff lacked empathy or made diagnostic errors, the majority report dedicated, compassionate assistance."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "results",
      "sentiment": "mixed",
      "mentions": 15,
      "title": {
        "en": "Critical medical interventions and clinical outcomes"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Numerous reviewers credit the clinic with saving pets during severe emergencies, including breathing crises, toxicities, and urgent foreign body removals. Clients value prompt diagnostic testing, such as ultrasounds and blood panels. However, several owners report distressed outcomes, mentioning misdiagnosed conditions, plasma delays, or prolonged diagnostic uncertainty during acute episodes."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "animals",
      "sentiment": "positive",
      "mentions": 9,
      "title": {
        "en": "Gentle handling during urgent assessments"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Pet owners consistently note how gently veterinarians and nurses handle anxious dogs and frail cats in acute distress. Reviewers appreciate that the team provides oxygen therapy, warm blankets, and soothing contact to minimise panic during examinations. One client noted a carrier safety mishap, but most clients commend the thoughtful physical care given to vulnerable pets."
      }
    }
  ],
  "faq": [
